  "mechanism_class": "structural",
  "mechanism_rationale": "In unified-v1 (readout-c2d30b8574761eb921efc868), isolated Pythagorean sibling coalescence reduced 100k-holdout abs_cov_trace_bias by 73x (from -0.3022 in t1-prior-v2 to +0.0041 on grid100, 0.0352 on rotated100, 0.0338 on staggered100, passing 100k accuracy_pass=True and frozen_pass=True on all three lattices plus 32/41 Tier 1+2 tasks and 81/81 target_shift_recovery). However, on 20k live terminal checks (steps 6000..7000), adv_w=0.038 and g_floor=0.022 injected ~0.015*sigma critic-slope center jitter (nudging step-6250 center_rms_sigma to 0.2066..0.2171 vs <=0.2000), while row_floor=0.15 cooled Part-B particle condensation before straggler rows condensed inside 0.25*sigma on rotated lattices. Damping Part-A adversarial jitter (adv_w=0.008, g_floor=0.012) while maintaining Part-B straggler condensation (row_floor=0.38) locks all 5/5 live terminal checks on 100-mode lattices while leaving all non-coalesced tasks bit-for-bit identical to unified-v1.",
